{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012K2WGMHJV841QcCcVxTvPf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3c33f1642e679c593e4860e9e529e55c5b74645e","date":"2026-09-10T21:01:00.000Z","author":"solomonfortune","subject":"(chore) O3-5964: Remove unreferenced SCSS files and dead AllergyFormTab component (#3638)","message":"(chore) O3-5964: Remove unreferenced SCSS files and dead AllergyFormTab component (#3638)","ticketKeys":["O3-5964"],"pullRequests":[3638],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T20:29:42.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\n\n* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers a","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3612],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app","hash":"120d22e968d57a1ce47a5a908e50e79f485cfcb1","date":"2026-06-11T12:24:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)\n\nThe allergy '+' control in the order basket's drug search falls back to\nlaunching the patient chart's allergy form workspace when the host does\nnot provide a launcher. The fill prescription workflow renders the order\nbasket outside the patient chart, so that fallback opened the\npatient-chart workspace group with null group props and crashed every\naction button registered to it with 'Cannot read properties of null\n(reading patientUuid)'.\n\nRegister the exported allergy form workspace from the allergies app into\nthe fill-prescription-window and pass its name as\nallergyFormWorkspaceName in the order basket window props, so the form\nopens as a child of the dispensing app's own workspace window. This is\nthe same wiring the ward app added in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2561 after the form was decoupled\nfrom the chart group in openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3353.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[854],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"160e8d0bc956f1e4d774a4a7f1047c06b8f18fda","date":"2026-06-04T17:50:57.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the order basket outside the patient chart (#3353)","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the order basket outside the patient chart (#3353)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3353],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6de29927bd14a8cbe34db3aa522b14e2f4ef8df4","date":"2026-04-07T13:47:10.000Z","author":"Shravanthi","subject":"(feat) O3-5540: Add quick-add allergy action to drug order basket (#3186)","message":"(feat) O3-5540: Add quick-add allergy action to drug order basket (#3186)","ticketKeys":["O3-5540"],"pullRequests":[3186],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"72a1cd76ef5f2f4beb6351c9c21f8305b4e8c92b","date":"2026-03-19T12:14:40.000Z","author":"omeri innocent","subject":"(fix) O3-5512: Re-enable allergy delete button after failed deletion (#3132)","message":"(fix) O3-5512: Re-enable allergy delete button after failed deletion (#3132)","ticketKeys":["O3-5512"],"pullRequests":[3132],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ac1012bafec8f832c80d5557bc5e818f8e2143ee","date":"2026-03-04T19:01:35.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)","message":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)\n\n* (fix) Improve E2E test reliability\n\nReplace fragile locators and fix test infrastructure issues that cause\nintermittent E2E failures.\n\nSelectors:\n- Replace .nth(0) positional selectors with row-scoped locators\n  (dataRow, getByRole('row').filter()) across allergies, biometrics,\n  conditions, drug-orders, lab-orders, results-viewer, visit-note, and\n  vitals specs\n- Replace CSS class selectors ([class*=\"previewContainer\"]) with\n  role-based locators in attachment preview tests\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for form input fields in\n  drug-orders\n- Add role=\"dialog\" and aria-label to attachment preview component\n  for stable test targeting\n\nAssertions:\n- Replace snapshot assertions (textContent + expect) with auto-retrying\n  Playwright assertions (toHaveText, toHaveValue) in edit-existing-visit\n- Wrap bare .isVisible() calls with expect() in immunizations\n- Add missing await on visitsPage.goTo() in results-viewer\n- Remove swallowed .catch(() => {}) on assertion in attachments\n\nTest state:\n- Convert module-level mutable state to per-test fixtures in\n  drug-orders and lab-orders specs (retry/parallel safe)\n- Use test patient fixture instead of manual creation in\n  visit-context-navigation\n- Add try/finally with null guards for cleanup of manually created\n  resources\n\nCleanup helpers:\n- Add response status assertions to deleteEncounter, deleteDrugOrder,\n  deleteTestOrder (accept 200/204/400/404/500)\n- Add ok() assertion to endVisit (accept 200/400 for already-ended\n  visits) and getVisit\n- Remove unnecessary empty request bodies from delete helpers\n\nDrug order recording:\n- Handle environment differences where the order basket may open the\n  drug search workspace directly or require an additional click\n\n* Drop status assertions from delete cleanup helpers\n\nDelete helpers are teardown code — they shouldn't fail the test if the\nresource was already removed or modified by the test itself. Asserting\non an ever-growing allowl","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3067],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"8ea84c53605bd7fcba910cbef4a9d187972d8816","date":"2026-02-26T17:14:13.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Remove redundant style overrides from allergy tags (#3063)","message":"(fix) Remove redundant style overrides from allergy tags (#3063)\n\nThe .allergyLabel class was overriding several Carbon Tag defaults\nunnecessarily: display, border-radius, text-align, and padding. It also\nset margin on each tag while the parent container already used\ncolumn-gap, tripling the effective spacing between tags (~12px instead\nof 4px).\n\nRemove all redundant overrides so allergy tags use Carbon's native Tag\nlayout, keeping only the severity-based background colors. Switch the\nparent container from column-gap to gap so wrapped rows are also spaced\ncorrectly.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3063],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6cd944f7d5c35862d6071c682ed3eb1223108801","date":"2026-02-12T23:14:54.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) Add allergy pills display to drug search","message":"(feat) Add allergy pills display to drug search\n\n- Add ExtensionSlot for allergy-list-pills-slot above search input\n- Add margin spacing to search input for better visual separation\n- Reorder Search component props alphabetically for consistency","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"54ddf9e5ecca4dc7e239e7362158ed58ee6fbc70","date":"2025-11-04T08:21:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Use correct translation namespace in allergies list extension","message":"(fix) Use correct translation namespace in allergies list extension\n\nFixes cross-app translation namespace for the allergies list extension\nby using the `translateFrom` function with the `moduleName` as the first\nargument instead of the `useTranslation` hook. This ensures that the translation\nstrings are loaded from the allergies app's namespace when the extension is\nrendered in other apps (e.g., medications app via the `allergy-list-pills-slot`\nextension slot).\n\nIt also removes unused `translateFrom` imports from conditions, lists, and\nprograms apps.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"9ab7d33918eabc27c31a0833f21c4da34f0298bf","date":"2025-10-28T18:30:22.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Add consistent spacing to allergies list extension","message":"(fix) Add consistent spacing to allergies list extension\n\nThis applies vertical spacing (spacing-03) and horizontal spacing (spacing-05)\naround the allergies list component, making it visually consistent with other\nUI elements in the patient chart.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"2fe74812c3a01b8c2ad556bc9e2312ded79cee59","date":"2025-10-11T16:42:54.000Z","author":"praneeth","subject":"(feat) O3-5094: Add severity-based sorting and visual indicators for allergies (#2777)","message":"(feat) O3-5094: Add severity-based sorting and visual indicators for allergies (#2777)\n\n* feat:implemented color coded severity indicator for allergies\n\n* updated\n\n* sorted tags\n\n* updated suggestion\n\n* Add tests and tweak a couple of things\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5094"],"pullRequests":[2777],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f6f1914aac0316723c5f91c4a06b394c93aa01ca","date":"2025-09-22T11:06:21.000Z","author":"Matt South","subject":"(feat) O3-5026: Allergy UI in Orders workflow (#2744)","message":"(feat) O3-5026: Allergy UI in Orders workflow (#2744)\n\n* placeholder for allergy pills in drug order form\n\n* allergies-list component\n\n* use carbon tag component\n\n* O3-5026 Allergy UI in Orders workflow\n\n* 3/4 of changes suggested in review\n\n* 4/4 of changes suggested in review\n\n* Additional tweaks to allergy components\n\n- Rename allergy components to use .extension.tsx suffix following OpenMRS conventions\n- Update component names for consistency (allergiesTile, allergiesList)\n- Improve loading states with `TagSkeleton`\n- Add red tag styling for allergy visibility in medication workflow\n- Standardize \"Unknown\" fallback text across components\n- Adapt the delete allergy modal registration logic in the routes.json file","ticketKeys":["O3-5026"],"pullRequests":[2744],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b80ac03cf23adfab5e0e57a2f6bc5e3591e89352","date":"2025-06-17T14:26:27.000Z","author":"praneeth","subject":"(feat) O3-3626: Allergen fields should be read-only when editing existing allergies  (#2462)","message":"(feat) O3-3626: Allergen fields should be read-only when editing existing allergies  (#2462)\n\n* feat: Add disabled state for allergens in allergy form and update styles\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* Make fields read-only on edit\n\n* Delete unused style\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-3626"],"pullRequests":[2462],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"acc0a71c4c382f8617d057ec9fd616aee6a6e828","date":"2025-06-03T16:55:39.000Z","author":"Michael Seaton","subject":"(fix) O3-4777 - Allergies tab does not display coded allergens (#2484)","message":"(fix) O3-4777 - Allergies tab does not display coded allergens (#2484)","ticketKeys":["O3-4777"],"pullRequests":[2484],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"dcd9635afa0e616c324ef9b7f138d1bcfc6368cd","date":"2025-04-08T10:06:59.000Z","author":"Dhruv Chandak","subject":"(refactor) O3-4604: Consolidate type annotations in the allergies widget (#2342)","message":"(refactor) O3-4604: Consolidate type annotations in the allergies widget (#2342)\n\n* refactor: centralize and reuse type definitions in types.ts for better consistency\n\n* fixed import statements\n\n* Consolidated imports\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-4604"],"pullRequests":[2342],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"0934dea3a70826d19fb50cb3b4a4616738f12d57","date":"2025-04-07T16:04:20.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Use correct a11y role for allergen combobox selector","message":"(test) Use correct a11y role for allergen combobox selector","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c038e67d4158fdf680ff1aadaad43a841a33f4c0","date":"2025-04-07T12:58:20.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(refactor) Improve allergy form initialization and loading states (#2347)","message":"(refactor) Improve allergy form initialization and loading states (#2347)\n\nThis commit addresses a critical issue where the allergy form would initialize with incorrect values when editing existing allergies. The problem occurred because:\n\n- Form initialization happened before allergic reactions were loaded from the server\n- Default values were only set once during form initialization\n- No loading state was shown while data was being fetched\n\nKey changes in this PR include:\n\n- Adding a loading state to the form that waits for allergic reactions to be loaded before initializing default values and rendering the form\n- Adding a ref to track initialization state to prevent the form from being rendered with incorrect values\n- Sorting the allergic reactions alphabetically by display name for improved readability and consistency\n- Adding a `CheckboxSkeleton` loading state to the form when allergic reactions are being loaded to prevent large layout shifts\n- Cleaning up the default value initialization logic for improved readability and maintainability","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2347],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"56861a24e4dcd9f52278e30cf7cd9293d78e4725","date":"2025-04-04T13:55:26.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic (#2333)","message":"(feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic (#2333)\n\n* (feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic\n\nThis PR centralizes validation logic in the allergies form workspace so that the\nzod schema is the source of truth for validation rules. Presently, some validation logic exists in useEffect\nhooks that determines whether the submit button should be disabled. This logic isn't tied to any display logic, which means\nthat validation errors are not shown to the user when they are encountered.\n\nWith this PR, fields are validated when the user attempts to save or update an allergy. If validation fails, the user is presented with\nthe appropriate error message.\n\n* Update tests to account for new allergy form validation\n\nThis commit updates the AllergyForm test suite to account for the new allergy form validation logic. It also effects some useful refactoring to the allergy form workspace component. Notably, that includes inlining the AllergicReactionsForm component, annotating the zod schema with useful comments, and replacing enums with constants in line with best practices.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2333],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8908349f0bab19860464c382ba2f86e92928629","date":"2025-04-02T19:35:46.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(fix) Allergies form should not change value to undefined (#2329)","message":"(fix) Allergies form should not change value to undefined (#2329)\n\nIn the E2E tests, when Playwright clicks on the allergen, two __item_clicked__ state changes are fired by Downshift (the library Carbon uses to implement the ComboBox). The first time this is fired, the selectedItem property is properly set to a value, but the second time it's set to `undefined`. Here we catch any attempts to set the value to `undefined` in the ComboBox onChange() handler and don't update the form state. However, clicking the button to clear the entry appears to send `null`, so this still works. This does lose the functionality where clicking on an already-selected item deselects that item (since that sets the current value to `undefined`), but that feels like a reasonable tradeoff.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2329],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"893e6ee0e80a0a7b50ba42f09de32b5d33ad2e11","date":"2025-03-26T10:09:29.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) Switch back to Chromium headless browser and update Playwright","message":"(chore) Switch back to Chromium headless browser and update Playwright\n\nSwitches the Playwright browser back to Chromium and updates the Playwright version. Unfortunately, there are some new Firefox-specific test failures owing to the Datepicker\ncomponent failing to set dates correctly. On the other hand, it looks like the Allergies e2e test passes when running on Firefox.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"60bea98198ca6c2e3dc7ac53b18b67eb4c7cb127","date":"2025-03-26T09:32:24.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) Run E2E tests on Firefox","message":"(chore) Run E2E tests on Firefox\n\nChanges the browser configuration in the Playwright test setup from Chrome to Firefox. This is an attempt to try and get a handle on the failing allergies e2e test. In my local testing,\nI've found that the test passes when running on Firefox. This change will help me get a better understanding of the issue.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f04eb533fce1cf9d86174ac67c2d300cc0f711d7","date":"2025-03-25T08:05:51.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Update allergen selector combobox label","message":"(test) Update allergen selector combobox label","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3a23cab4d22c927bc2c6b2da8939151f3c75f926","date":"2025-03-25T07:47:00.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Improve allergen selector robustness in allergies form e2e test","message":"(test) Improve allergen selector robustness in allergies form e2e test\n\nSwitches to using a role-based selector instead of placeholder text for the allergen selector.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"0e206391af809d9cb73a0440632d34277dff7f61","date":"2025-03-15T17:23:50.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Improve selector reliability in conditions test","message":"(test) Improve selector reliability in conditions test\n\nReplace generic text-based selector with more specific role+filter selector\nfor selecting the \"All\" option in the conditions dropdown menu.\nThis makes the test more precise by ensuring it clicks on the correct\noption element rather than any element containing the text \"all\", such as the Allergies dashboard link.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"548f8afcf734e0c7fbb87d6345e2490a528994cf","date":"2025-02-14T13:04:29.000Z","author":"praneeth","subject":"(feat) O3-4342: Split allergy form fields (#2232)","message":"(feat) O3-4342: Split allergy form fields (#2232)\n\n* added openmrs datepicker\n\n* Improve error handling for comments in AllergyForm\n\n* replace openmrsDatePicker with cabon design datepicker\n\n* remove the onsetDate and kept only the comments\n\n* Correct label text casing for comments field in allergy form\n\n* updated en.json\n\n* updated en.json\n\n* fixup\n\n* removed onset date text in allergies.spec.ts\n\n* Rename 'comment' to 'comments' in allergy form schema and related logic\n\n* Refactor allergy form styling and improve form submission logic\n\n- Adds a loading state to the submit button when the form is being submitted\n- Fixes the form height to ensure the action buttons are pinned to the bottom of the form\n- Changes the `comments` form field name back to `comment` to match the backend data model\n- Fixes an issue where the allergic reactions from an existing allergy record were not correctly loaded into the form\nwhen editing.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-4342"],"pullRequests":[2232],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"5cab0737fca2e515f24eb53dbf1d2639519c0a26","date":"2025-01-28T13:17:28.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(fix) O3-4403: Unable to record allergy in non-English locale (#2215)","message":"(fix) O3-4403: Unable to record allergy in non-English locale (#2215)\n\n* (fix) Unable to record allergy in non-English locale\r\n\r\n* Remove index","ticketKeys":["O3-4403"],"pullRequests":[2215],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["allerg"],"count":30},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: showing 30 of 33 found","commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 27 of 33 found"]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1144e896-b83d-4ef0-bfdc-6120d4e22450","uuid":"89bc7b77-d1da-4948-b8dc-ebed1c088c40","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:35:15.696Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3c33f1642e679c593e4860e9e529e55c5b74645e","date":"2026-09-10T21:01:00.000Z","author":"solomonfortune","subject":"(chore) O3-5964: Remove unreferenced SCSS files and dead AllergyFormTab component (#3638)","message":"(chore) O3-5964: Remove unreferenced SCSS files and dead AllergyFormTab component (#3638)","ticketKeys":["O3-5964"],"pullRequests":[3638],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T20:29:42.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\n\n* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers a","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3612],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app","hash":"120d22e968d57a1ce47a5a908e50e79f485cfcb1","date":"2026-06-11T12:24:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)\n\nThe allergy '+' control in the order basket's drug search falls back to\nlaunching the patient chart's allergy form workspace when the host does\nnot provide a launcher. The fill prescription workflow renders the order\nbasket outside the patient chart, so that fallback opened the\npatient-chart workspace group with null group props and crashed every\naction button registered to it with 'Cannot read properties of null\n(reading patientUuid)'.\n\nRegister the exported allergy form workspace from the allergies app into\nthe fill-prescription-window and pass its name as\nallergyFormWorkspaceName in the order basket window props, so the form\nopens as a child of the dispensing app's own workspace window. This is\nthe same wiring the ward app added in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2561 after the form was decoupled\nfrom the chart group in openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3353.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[854],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"160e8d0bc956f1e4d774a4a7f1047c06b8f18fda","date":"2026-06-04T17:50:57.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the order basket outside the patient chart (#3353)","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the order basket outside the patient chart (#3353)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3353],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6de29927bd14a8cbe34db3aa522b14e2f4ef8df4","date":"2026-04-07T13:47:10.000Z","author":"Shravanthi","subject":"(feat) O3-5540: Add quick-add allergy action to drug order basket (#3186)","message":"(feat) O3-5540: Add quick-add allergy action to drug order basket (#3186)","ticketKeys":["O3-5540"],"pullRequests":[3186],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"72a1cd76ef5f2f4beb6351c9c21f8305b4e8c92b","date":"2026-03-19T12:14:40.000Z","author":"omeri innocent","subject":"(fix) O3-5512: Re-enable allergy delete button after failed deletion (#3132)","message":"(fix) O3-5512: Re-enable allergy delete button after failed deletion (#3132)","ticketKeys":["O3-5512"],"pullRequests":[3132],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ac1012bafec8f832c80d5557bc5e818f8e2143ee","date":"2026-03-04T19:01:35.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)","message":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)\n\n* (fix) Improve E2E test reliability\n\nReplace fragile locators and fix test infrastructure issues that cause\nintermittent E2E failures.\n\nSelectors:\n- Replace .nth(0) positional selectors with row-scoped locators\n  (dataRow, getByRole('row').filter()) across allergies, biometrics,\n  conditions, drug-orders, lab-orders, results-viewer, visit-note, and\n  vitals specs\n- Replace CSS class selectors ([class*=\"previewContainer\"]) with\n  role-based locators in attachment preview tests\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for form input fields in\n  drug-orders\n- Add role=\"dialog\" and aria-label to attachment preview component\n  for stable test targeting\n\nAssertions:\n- Replace snapshot assertions (textContent + expect) with auto-retrying\n  Playwright assertions (toHaveText, toHaveValue) in edit-existing-visit\n- Wrap bare .isVisible() calls with expect() in immunizations\n- Add missing await on visitsPage.goTo() in results-viewer\n- Remove swallowed .catch(() => {}) on assertion in attachments\n\nTest state:\n- Convert module-level mutable state to per-test fixtures in\n  drug-orders and lab-orders specs (retry/parallel safe)\n- Use test patient fixture instead of manual creation in\n  visit-context-navigation\n- Add try/finally with null guards for cleanup of manually created\n  resources\n\nCleanup helpers:\n- Add response status assertions to deleteEncounter, deleteDrugOrder,\n  deleteTestOrder (accept 200/204/400/404/500)\n- Add ok() assertion to endVisit (accept 200/400 for already-ended\n  visits) and getVisit\n- Remove unnecessary empty request bodies from delete helpers\n\nDrug order recording:\n- Handle environment differences where the order basket may open the\n  drug search workspace directly or require an additional click\n\n* Drop status assertions from delete cleanup helpers\n\nDelete helpers are teardown code — they shouldn't fail the test if the\nresource was already removed or modified by the test itself. Asserting\non an ever-growing allowl","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3067],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"8ea84c53605bd7fcba910cbef4a9d187972d8816","date":"2026-02-26T17:14:13.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Remove redundant style overrides from allergy tags (#3063)","message":"(fix) Remove redundant style overrides from allergy tags (#3063)\n\nThe .allergyLabel class was overriding several Carbon Tag defaults\nunnecessarily: display, border-radius, text-align, and padding. It also\nset margin on each tag while the parent container already used\ncolumn-gap, tripling the effective spacing between tags (~12px instead\nof 4px).\n\nRemove all redundant overrides so allergy tags use Carbon's native Tag\nlayout, keeping only the severity-based background colors. Switch the\nparent container from column-gap to gap so wrapped rows are also spaced\ncorrectly.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3063],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6cd944f7d5c35862d6071c682ed3eb1223108801","date":"2026-02-12T23:14:54.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) Add allergy pills display to drug search","message":"(feat) Add allergy pills display to drug search\n\n- Add ExtensionSlot for allergy-list-pills-slot above search input\n- Add margin spacing to search input for better visual separation\n- Reorder Search component props alphabetically for consistency","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"54ddf9e5ecca4dc7e239e7362158ed58ee6fbc70","date":"2025-11-04T08:21:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Use correct translation namespace in allergies list extension","message":"(fix) Use correct translation namespace in allergies list extension\n\nFixes cross-app translation namespace for the allergies list extension\nby using the `translateFrom` function with the `moduleName` as the first\nargument instead of the `useTranslation` hook. This ensures that the translation\nstrings are loaded from the allergies app's namespace when the extension is\nrendered in other apps (e.g., medications app via the `allergy-list-pills-slot`\nextension slot).\n\nIt also removes unused `translateFrom` imports from conditions, lists, and\nprograms apps.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"9ab7d33918eabc27c31a0833f21c4da34f0298bf","date":"2025-10-28T18:30:22.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Add consistent spacing to allergies list extension","message":"(fix) Add consistent spacing to allergies list extension\n\nThis applies vertical spacing (spacing-03) and horizontal spacing (spacing-05)\naround the allergies list component, making it visually consistent with other\nUI elements in the patient chart.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"2fe74812c3a01b8c2ad556bc9e2312ded79cee59","date":"2025-10-11T16:42:54.000Z","author":"praneeth","subject":"(feat) O3-5094: Add severity-based sorting and visual indicators for allergies (#2777)","message":"(feat) O3-5094: Add severity-based sorting and visual indicators for allergies (#2777)\n\n* feat:implemented color coded severity indicator for allergies\n\n* updated\n\n* sorted tags\n\n* updated suggestion\n\n* Add tests and tweak a couple of things\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5094"],"pullRequests":[2777],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f6f1914aac0316723c5f91c4a06b394c93aa01ca","date":"2025-09-22T11:06:21.000Z","author":"Matt South","subject":"(feat) O3-5026: Allergy UI in Orders workflow (#2744)","message":"(feat) O3-5026: Allergy UI in Orders workflow (#2744)\n\n* placeholder for allergy pills in drug order form\n\n* allergies-list component\n\n* use carbon tag component\n\n* O3-5026 Allergy UI in Orders workflow\n\n* 3/4 of changes suggested in review\n\n* 4/4 of changes suggested in review\n\n* Additional tweaks to allergy components\n\n- Rename allergy components to use .extension.tsx suffix following OpenMRS conventions\n- Update component names for consistency (allergiesTile, allergiesList)\n- Improve loading states with `TagSkeleton`\n- Add red tag styling for allergy visibility in medication workflow\n- Standardize \"Unknown\" fallback text across components\n- Adapt the delete allergy modal registration logic in the routes.json file","ticketKeys":["O3-5026"],"pullRequests":[2744],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b80ac03cf23adfab5e0e57a2f6bc5e3591e89352","date":"2025-06-17T14:26:27.000Z","author":"praneeth","subject":"(feat) O3-3626: Allergen fields should be read-only when editing existing allergies  (#2462)","message":"(feat) O3-3626: Allergen fields should be read-only when editing existing allergies  (#2462)\n\n* feat: Add disabled state for allergens in allergy form and update styles\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* Make fields read-only on edit\n\n* Delete unused style\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-3626"],"pullRequests":[2462],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"acc0a71c4c382f8617d057ec9fd616aee6a6e828","date":"2025-06-03T16:55:39.000Z","author":"Michael Seaton","subject":"(fix) O3-4777 - Allergies tab does not display coded allergens (#2484)","message":"(fix) O3-4777 - Allergies tab does not display coded allergens (#2484)","ticketKeys":["O3-4777"],"pullRequests":[2484],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"dcd9635afa0e616c324ef9b7f138d1bcfc6368cd","date":"2025-04-08T10:06:59.000Z","author":"Dhruv Chandak","subject":"(refactor) O3-4604: Consolidate type annotations in the allergies widget (#2342)","message":"(refactor) O3-4604: Consolidate type annotations in the allergies widget (#2342)\n\n* refactor: centralize and reuse type definitions in types.ts for better consistency\n\n* fixed import statements\n\n* Consolidated imports\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-4604"],"pullRequests":[2342],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"0934dea3a70826d19fb50cb3b4a4616738f12d57","date":"2025-04-07T16:04:20.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Use correct a11y role for allergen combobox selector","message":"(test) Use correct a11y role for allergen combobox selector","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c038e67d4158fdf680ff1aadaad43a841a33f4c0","date":"2025-04-07T12:58:20.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(refactor) Improve allergy form initialization and loading states (#2347)","message":"(refactor) Improve allergy form initialization and loading states (#2347)\n\nThis commit addresses a critical issue where the allergy form would initialize with incorrect values when editing existing allergies. The problem occurred because:\n\n- Form initialization happened before allergic reactions were loaded from the server\n- Default values were only set once during form initialization\n- No loading state was shown while data was being fetched\n\nKey changes in this PR include:\n\n- Adding a loading state to the form that waits for allergic reactions to be loaded before initializing default values and rendering the form\n- Adding a ref to track initialization state to prevent the form from being rendered with incorrect values\n- Sorting the allergic reactions alphabetically by display name for improved readability and consistency\n- Adding a `CheckboxSkeleton` loading state to the form when allergic reactions are being loaded to prevent large layout shifts\n- Cleaning up the default value initialization logic for improved readability and maintainability","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2347],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"56861a24e4dcd9f52278e30cf7cd9293d78e4725","date":"2025-04-04T13:55:26.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic (#2333)","message":"(feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic (#2333)\n\n* (feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic\n\nThis PR centralizes validation logic in the allergies form workspace so that the\nzod schema is the source of truth for validation rules. Presently, some validation logic exists in useEffect\nhooks that determines whether the submit button should be disabled. This logic isn't tied to any display logic, which means\nthat validation errors are not shown to the user when they are encountered.\n\nWith this PR, fields are validated when the user attempts to save or update an allergy. If validation fails, the user is presented with\nthe appropriate error message.\n\n* Update tests to account for new allergy form validation\n\nThis commit updates the AllergyForm test suite to account for the new allergy form validation logic. It also effects some useful refactoring to the allergy form workspace component. Notably, that includes inlining the AllergicReactionsForm component, annotating the zod schema with useful comments, and replacing enums with constants in line with best practices.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2333],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8908349f0bab19860464c382ba2f86e92928629","date":"2025-04-02T19:35:46.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(fix) Allergies form should not change value to undefined (#2329)","message":"(fix) Allergies form should not change value to undefined (#2329)\n\nIn the E2E tests, when Playwright clicks on the allergen, two __item_clicked__ state changes are fired by Downshift (the library Carbon uses to implement the ComboBox). The first time this is fired, the selectedItem property is properly set to a value, but the second time it's set to `undefined`. Here we catch any attempts to set the value to `undefined` in the ComboBox onChange() handler and don't update the form state. However, clicking the button to clear the entry appears to send `null`, so this still works. This does lose the functionality where clicking on an already-selected item deselects that item (since that sets the current value to `undefined`), but that feels like a reasonable tradeoff.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2329],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"893e6ee0e80a0a7b50ba42f09de32b5d33ad2e11","date":"2025-03-26T10:09:29.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) Switch back to Chromium headless browser and update Playwright","message":"(chore) Switch back to Chromium headless browser and update Playwright\n\nSwitches the Playwright browser back to Chromium and updates the Playwright version. Unfortunately, there are some new Firefox-specific test failures owing to the Datepicker\ncomponent failing to set dates correctly. On the other hand, it looks like the Allergies e2e test passes when running on Firefox.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"60bea98198ca6c2e3dc7ac53b18b67eb4c7cb127","date":"2025-03-26T09:32:24.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) Run E2E tests on Firefox","message":"(chore) Run E2E tests on Firefox\n\nChanges the browser configuration in the Playwright test setup from Chrome to Firefox. This is an attempt to try and get a handle on the failing allergies e2e test. In my local testing,\nI've found that the test passes when running on Firefox. This change will help me get a better understanding of the issue.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f04eb533fce1cf9d86174ac67c2d300cc0f711d7","date":"2025-03-25T08:05:51.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Update allergen selector combobox label","message":"(test) Update allergen selector combobox label","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3a23cab4d22c927bc2c6b2da8939151f3c75f926","date":"2025-03-25T07:47:00.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Improve allergen selector robustness in allergies form e2e test","message":"(test) Improve allergen selector robustness in allergies form e2e test\n\nSwitches to using a role-based selector instead of placeholder text for the allergen selector.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"0e206391af809d9cb73a0440632d34277dff7f61","date":"2025-03-15T17:23:50.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Improve selector reliability in conditions test","message":"(test) Improve selector reliability in conditions test\n\nReplace generic text-based selector with more specific role+filter selector\nfor selecting the \"All\" option in the conditions dropdown menu.\nThis makes the test more precise by ensuring it clicks on the correct\noption element rather than any element containing the text \"all\", such as the Allergies dashboard link.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"548f8afcf734e0c7fbb87d6345e2490a528994cf","date":"2025-02-14T13:04:29.000Z","author":"praneeth","subject":"(feat) O3-4342: Split allergy form fields (#2232)","message":"(feat) O3-4342: Split allergy form fields (#2232)\n\n* added openmrs datepicker\n\n* Improve error handling for comments in AllergyForm\n\n* replace openmrsDatePicker with cabon design datepicker\n\n* remove the onsetDate and kept only the comments\n\n* Correct label text casing for comments field in allergy form\n\n* updated en.json\n\n* updated en.json\n\n* fixup\n\n* removed onset date text in allergies.spec.ts\n\n* Rename 'comment' to 'comments' in allergy form schema and related logic\n\n* Refactor allergy form styling and improve form submission logic\n\n- Adds a loading state to the submit button when the form is being submitted\n- Fixes the form height to ensure the action buttons are pinned to the bottom of the form\n- Changes the `comments` form field name back to `comment` to match the backend data model\n- Fixes an issue where the allergic reactions from an existing allergy record were not correctly loaded into the form\nwhen editing.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-4342"],"pullRequests":[2232],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"5cab0737fca2e515f24eb53dbf1d2639519c0a26","date":"2025-01-28T13:17:28.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(fix) O3-4403: Unable to record allergy in non-English locale (#2215)","message":"(fix) O3-4403: Unable to record allergy in non-English locale (#2215)\n\n* (fix) Unable to record allergy in non-English locale\r\n\r\n* Remove index","ticketKeys":["O3-4403"],"pullRequests":[2215],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["allerg"],"count":30},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: showing 30 of 33 found","commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 27 of 33 found"]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012K2WGMHJV841QcCcVxTvPf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
