{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G52cgs2BJBGkAF6a3Xp1zc","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"5ffb3aab5567d5687d08a9029dc0d1edeea45e31","date":"2026-06-17T11:44:02.000Z","author":"Souravjyoti Dutta","subject":"(fix) O3-5739: Decode HTML entities in sticky note content to render special characters correctly (#3383)","message":"(fix) O3-5739: Decode HTML entities in sticky note content to render special characters correctly (#3383)\n\n* fix encoding issue\n\n* mock\n\n* (refactor) O3-5739: Use textarea-based HTML entity decoding, move to utils\n\nReplace the DOMParser-based decodeHtmlEntities with a detached <textarea>,\nwhich decodes character references without parsing tags or hoisting head\ncontent. Move the helper out of sticky-note.resource.ts into a feature-scoped\nutils.ts, and decode the existing note value once in the modal instead of on\nevery keystroke.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor using html-entites\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: NethmiRodrigo <nethmi.dilinika@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5739"],"pullRequests":[3383],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"a3c434ef4821087bb58556d4a200e4f6fb966b51","date":"2026-06-15T06:42:26.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) O3-5738: Prevent spurious unsaved-changes prompt when starting a visit (#3381)","message":"(fix) O3-5738: Prevent spurious unsaved-changes prompt when starting a visit (#3381)\n\n(fix) Prevent spurious unsaved-changes prompt when starting a visit\n\nAfter the visit create/update request succeeds, the form no longer\nreports unsaved changes. Previously, the workspace stayed marked dirty\nwhile post-save extension callbacks (appointment check-in, billing)\nwere awaited, so the active-visit revalidation could relaunch the\npatient chart workspace group mid-flight and prompt the user to\ndiscard changes that were already saved.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5738"],"pullRequests":[3381],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app","hash":"120d22e968d57a1ce47a5a908e50e79f485cfcb1","date":"2026-06-11T12:24:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the fill prescription order basket (#854)\n\nThe allergy '+' control in the order basket's drug search falls back to\nlaunching the patient chart's allergy form workspace when the host does\nnot provide a launcher. The fill prescription workflow renders the order\nbasket outside the patient chart, so that fallback opened the\npatient-chart workspace group with null group props and crashed every\naction button registered to it with 'Cannot read properties of null\n(reading patientUuid)'.\n\nRegister the exported allergy form workspace from the allergies app into\nthe fill-prescription-window and pass its name as\nallergyFormWorkspaceName in the order basket window props, so the form\nopens as a child of the dispensing app's own workspace window. This is\nthe same wiring the ward app added in\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2561 after the form was decoupled\nfrom the chart group in openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart#3353.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[854],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"160e8d0bc956f1e4d774a4a7f1047c06b8f18fda","date":"2026-06-04T17:50:57.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the order basket outside the patient chart (#3353)","message":"(fix) Allow recording allergies from the order basket outside the patient chart (#3353)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3353],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"de10a557d158087f9a4697b84d4217f66a128958","date":"2026-06-04T11:42:44.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) O3-5722: Increase visit summary tab min-height to prevent content clipping (#3352)","message":"(fix) O3-5722: Increase visit summary tab min-height to prevent content clipping (#3352)","ticketKeys":["O3-5722"],"pullRequests":[3352],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app","hash":"c7cb239767abb84417c945bc4dfd476453f2e4e5","date":"2026-06-03T20:26:09.000Z","author":"chibongho","subject":"(fix) O3-5650: Subject results in the search tab to location filtering config (#843)","message":"(fix) O3-5650: Subject results in the search tab to location filtering config (#843)","ticketKeys":["O3-5650"],"pullRequests":[843],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"7e9e5ee856918aadc24ef5166218dec3fc800a62","date":"2026-05-27T21:42:35.000Z","author":"Dilan Kavishka","subject":"(test) O3-5655: Add E2E for procedure app (#3338)","message":"(test) O3-5655: Add E2E for procedure app (#3338)","ticketKeys":["O3-5655"],"pullRequests":[3338],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6797e139e35959962c51b4148213d88ccdc94af7","date":"2026-05-26T14:08:03.000Z","author":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","subject":"(feat) O3-5077: Support recording clinical procedures (#3320)","message":"(feat) O3-5077: Support recording clinical procedures (#3320)\n\n* Update pull request branches in CI workflow\n\nRemove main branch restriction from pull requests.\n\n* Remove 'patch/*' branch from CI trigger\n\n* Update CI workflow to include additional branches\n\n* Add esm-patient-procedures-app to patient-chart monorepo\n\n* Refactor the file structure\n\n* Add feat/procedure-history branch to workflow triggers\n\n* Modify E2E test triggers for additional branches\n\nUpdated branch filters for E2E tests on push and pull request events.\n\n* Make concept sources configurable\n\n* Load durations dynamically\n\n* Make the form wider\n\n* Make the duration unit combo box\n\n* Make status a combo box\n\n* (fix) O3-5656: Make submit buttons sticky on procedure history form (#3290)\n\n* Fix: stick the submit buttons in procedure form\n\n* Fix: update procedures-form.workspace.test.tsx to new ComboBox components\n\n* (fix) O3-5657: Various fixes to the procedures form (#3297)\n\n* (fix) O3-5653: Wire body site and status concepts in config schema (#3313)\n\n\n\nCo-authored-by: Jayasanka Weerasinghe <33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Cleanup the file structure\n\n* Migrate to vitest\n\n* Fix the workspace\n\n* Isolate date time component\n\n* Prevent future 'any' types\n\n* Convert all function declarations to arrow functions\n\n* Fix accessibility issues in ConceptSearchField (#15)\n\n* Clear slected concep when changing value\n\n* Re-enable delete button after failed delete\n\nsetIsDeleting(false) was missing from the catch block, leaving\nthe Delete button permanently disabled after a transient error.\nUser had to close and reopen the modal to retry.\n\nAlso updates the test assertion to verify the button is re-enabled\nafter an error so the user can retry without reopening the modal.\n\n* docs: add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Add README for esm-patient-procedures-app\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Enable delete button on error\n\n* Rename file\n\n* Add separate pagination configs for overview and detailed view\n\n* Ali","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-5077","O3-5656","O3-5657","O3-5653"],"pullRequests":[3320],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"7d2ad06a4c256c8c218923c7f6dfe65892aed981","date":"2026-05-26T10:40:05.000Z","author":"Donald Kibet","subject":"(fix) O3-5707: Relaunch patient chart workspace group when visit context changes (#3332)","message":"(fix) O3-5707: Relaunch patient chart workspace group when visit context changes (#3332)","ticketKeys":["O3-5707"],"pullRequests":[3332],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b8d3fe2ea7a8546c4f4800029bdaec4f6423a8c8","date":"2026-05-25T20:18:12.000Z","author":"Tanishq Sangwan","subject":"(feat) O3-5374: Add support for future medication start dates (#2973)","message":"(feat) O3-5374: Add support for future medication start dates (#2973)","ticketKeys":["O3-5374"],"pullRequests":[2973],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm